WEBVTT

00:01:14.150 --> 00:01:16.940
Washizu Mahjong, where defeat 
means total destruction.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:19.500
The genius from the 
darkness, Akagi Shigeru,

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.120
displayed that genius 
in the first two matches

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.360
and turned the flow of 
the game into his favor.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.130
In the third match, though, 
with his back against the wall,

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.400
Washizu showed his monster-like luck by 
evolving a trash hand to a haneman hand.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.800
Akagi is in a desperate situation.

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:40.440
The countdown to death is beginning.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:47.680
<i>One more tile.</i>

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:55.030
<i>I just need to draw one more 
tile and I can kill this man.</i>

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.450
<b>Episode 24</b>

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.450
<b>The Will of the Demons</b>

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:10.940
Akagi has lost 1,100 CCs 
of blood thus far.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:14.440
If Washizu draws his winning tile 
for a haneman, each player pays 6,000.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:19.070
It means Akagi will lose 
an additional 600 CCs.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.230
<i>That will put him one step 
away from the fatal amount.</i>

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:31.840
<i>Each and every tile Washizu draws is 
a potential death sentence for Akagi.</i>

00:02:34.430 --> 00:02:37.430
<i>Just one more, Akagi.</i>

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:43.170
<i>And then I'll be able to kill you.</i>

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.060
<i>I can kill you.</i>

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.730
<i>Your life right now is a 
veritable candle in the wind.</i>

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:57.950
<i>I can see it.</i>

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.920
<i>The flame of your life is about to die out.</i>

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.750
<i>That final flicker.</i>

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:16.770
This could be the very tile 
that extinguishes your life.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:21.770
<i>So... what's with him?</i>

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.280
<i>He's on the brink, 
so why is he so calm?</i>

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.280
Damn it!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.200
<i>This isn't fun at all.</i>

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.910
<i>It's only the ones around him who panic.</i>

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.040
<i>But the one who should panic most...</i>

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:57.040
<i>This punk... doesn't move a muscle.</i>

00:03:58.260 --> 00:03:59.770
<i>This isn't fun.</i>

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:02.280
<i>Why aren't you afraid?</i>

00:04:02.280 --> 00:04:04.650
<i>Why don't you tremble?</i>

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.480
<i>Do you think you won't die?</i>

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.290
<i>Do you think you cannot die?</i>

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.750
<i>Are you making light of all this?</i>

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:14.320
<i>You think it won't come to that?</i>

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:24.700
<i>So even if I draw my winning 
tile, without a reverse dora,</i>

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:28.660
<i>I'll have a riichi, tsumo, three 
dora, only a dealer mangan.</i>

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:31.910
<i>You're saying it won't 
go so far as a haneman?</i>

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.140
<i>No.</i>

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:39.620
<i>Even so, a mangan tsumo as dealer 
gets me 4,000 from each player.</i>

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.050
<i>Which means he'll have 
400 CCs of blood drawn.</i>

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:48.980
<i>Combined with his blood until 
now, that'll be 1,500 CCs.</i>

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.360
<i>He may not die from it, 
but he'll be at the very end!</i>

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:56.110
<i>He'll barely be alive after 
that much blood loss.</i>

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:57.630
<i>He'll be weaving.</i>

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:02.620
<i>In a half-dead state where he won't 
even be able to think clearly.</i>

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:06.170
<i>If he keeps playing in that state, 
a mistake is inevitable.</i>

00:05:06.170 --> 00:05:09.680
<i>In the end, he will die.</i>

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:13.040
<i>This is a self-evident truth.</i>

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.350
<i>It is impossible that you 
don't comprehend that.</i>

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:22.130
<i>So then, why don't you tremble?</i>

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:23.520
<i>Why?</i>

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.030
<i>Are you not afraid?</i>

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.260
<i>Of death?</i>

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.760
<i>Of dying?</i>

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.470
<i>Of dying?!</i>

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.760
<i>Of dying?!</i>

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:38.270
<i>Of dying?!</i>

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.000
<i>This cannot be.</i>

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.260
<i>Until now, every one of those 
worthless young punks who died here</i>

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:54.590
<i>cracked their masks when the 
moment of death became evident</i>

00:05:54.590 --> 00:06:00.690
<i>and showed me their true, fragile face.</i>

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.260
Stop it!

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:03.580
I don't want to die!

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:06.170
I don't want to die!

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.560
I don't want to die!

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:11.270
<i>It's that tenacious desire to live.</i>

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.680
<i>They know it cannot be fulfilled</i>

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.940
<i>and yet they cling to it.</i>

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:22.690
<i>And then they expire.</i>

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:28.420
<i>And yet, this lunatic...</i>

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.650
<i>Lunatic. Lunatic!</i>

00:06:31.650 --> 00:06:34.490
<i>This lunatic!</i>

00:06:35.510 --> 00:06:38.160
<i>He cannot be an exception.</i>

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.250
<i>That is simply not possible.</i>

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.830
<i>Washizu-sama.</i>

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:45.170
<i>What?</i>

00:06:45.830 --> 00:06:48.910
<i>I told you to not deal into my hand yet.</i>

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:51.600
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.060
<i>The 2 of circles?</i>

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.650
<i>You drew the fourth one?</i>

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.930
<i>This is fun.</i>

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:03.150
<i>Shall I?</i>

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:05.160
<i>Of course!</i>

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.060
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:09.230
Kan!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.520
Not again!

00:07:15.070 --> 00:07:17.130
It's East Hand 2, the 11th turn.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:19.230
Suzuki declares another kan.

00:07:20.290 --> 00:07:23.370
This concealed kan will add 
more support to Washizu.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:27.880
It's a greedy kan whose reverse 
doras could boost his hand even more.

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:37.500
It is fruitful.

00:07:42.830 --> 00:07:45.390
This means Washizu's hand 
has evolved yet again.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.130
1 of bamboo...

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:51.290
<i>The new dora is the 2 of bamboo.</i>

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:51.870
It morphs!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.100
Into a six-dora hand.

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:56.440
With a riichi, six dora,

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:58.510
his hand is now guaranteed 
to be a dealer's haneman.

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:02.740
Should he draw his winning tile 
or get even a single reverse dora,

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.730
his hand would go all the 
way to a dealer's baiman.

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:07.540
It is truly an exceptional situation.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:13.120
<i>What remarkable... luck!</i>

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.540
<i>It's surging forward...</i>

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.950
<i>Something... coming to 
elevate Washizu-sama.</i>

00:08:24.120 --> 00:08:26.320
<i>Something magical.</i>

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:32.930
<i>I feel it.</i>

00:08:32.930 --> 00:08:35.080
<i>I feel it now!</i>

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:40.580
<i>Is this powerful feeling... 
is it the will of the demons?</i>

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:49.330
<i>Washizu-sama, shall I discard it here?</i>

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.570
With the guaranteed dealer haneman,

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:54.690
the current flow of the game

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:57.770
suggests that the chance of 
getting a reverse dora is high.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:00.830
<i>Isn't this enough?</i>

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.070
You fool.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:06.840
<i>What are you saying?</i>

00:09:06.840 --> 00:09:09.080
<i>Why would I ever stop now?</i>

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:11.970
<i>Keep going, keep going!</i>

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:18.080
<i>If I draw the 1 of circles myself, 
I'll have a dealer baiman.</i>

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:20.790
<i>8,000 points from everyone.</i>

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:26.030
<i>I'll be able to steal another 
800 CCs of blood from him.</i>

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.060
<i>That will be a total of 1,900 CCs.</i>

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:36.300
<i>That amount of blood loss 
is certain death.</i>

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.590
<i>An amount that is absolutely fatal.</i>

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.810
<i>He will die!</i>

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:46.550
<i>With his death so imminent, 
even he must begin to tremble!</i>

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:51.280
<i>I must see it!</i>

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.790
<i>Show me that agony!</i>

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:56.550
<i>Tremble!</i>

00:09:56.550 --> 00:10:00.880
<i>Show me your despair!</i>

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:15.410
Keep going.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:21.880
<i>Now show me...</i>

00:10:21.880 --> 00:10:24.880
<i>Start trembling from 
despair and show me.</i>

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:29.000
<i>Under that mask of calm you wear,</i>

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:36.130
<i>show me your true, fragile self, 
convulsing in fear as you cling to life.</i>

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:42.860
<i>If you discard it, you will, 
undoubtedly, die.</i>

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:45.990
<i>Huh?</i>

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.100
<i>You put it in your hand again?</i>

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.160
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:54.610
<i>It seems like his hand is finally 
starting to get somewhere.</i>

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:59.120
<i>Looks like you finally got rid 
of most of your useless tiles.</i>

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:03.620
<i>So, will you finally get there,</i>

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:09.590
<i>to that 1 of circles?</i>

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:17.600
Suzuki's kan has completely 
used up all the 2 of circles tiles.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.260
This closed wait has no way 
of becoming a sequence.

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.340
The 3 of circles pair still has potential,

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.540
but the 1 of circles is 
definitely worthless now.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:31.850
<i>You'll never get into tenpai if 
you keep hanging on to that tile.</i>

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.850
<i>Why don't you discard it, Akagi?</i>

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:39.840
<i>Suzuki has a 1 of circles 
in his second discard pile,</i>

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:45.280
<i>and you might just be 
imagining that it's a trap.</i>

00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.860
<i>Huh, Akagi?</i>

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:51.290
<i>After all, that is what 
Mahjong is all about.</i>

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:54.870
<i>The 1 of circles might just pass.</i>

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:57.870
<i>Huh, Akagi?</i>

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.710
<i>What's this?</i>

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.350
<i>He still won't discard it?</i>

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.360
<i>Does he actually know?</i>

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.880
<i>Does he know I'm waiting 
for the 1 of circles?</i>

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:24.520
<i>That's fine.</i>

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:27.370
<i>That's fine, too.</i>

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:36.580
<i>It just means that I'll 
have to draw it for myself.</i>

00:12:37.220 --> 00:12:40.440
<i>You will die!</i>

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:49.210
<i>You will die!</i>

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:53.490
<i>You will die!</i>

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:57.000
<i>You will die!</i>

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:59.230
<i>You will die.</i>

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:04.140
<i>What is this?</i>

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.670
<i>Why don't you tremble?</i>

00:13:07.670 --> 00:13:10.720
<i>You will die from this draw...</i>

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:13.620
<i>Once I draw it...</i>

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:25.660
<i>Again, the only ones who seem 
afraid are those around him.</i>

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:29.900
<i>And still, you've yet to move a muscle.</i>

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:31.180
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:31.180 --> 00:13:32.610
<i>Why?!</i>

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:43.870
<i>What is this draw?</i>

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.340
<i>This flow?</i>

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.850
Unbelievably, he is now at eight dora!

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:52.320
Kan!

00:14:02.140 --> 00:14:07.000
By delaying Suzuki from dealing 
into his hand immediately,

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.770
Washizu's hand develops 
in an unexpected way.

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:23.250
<i>The demons have finally 
taken possession of me.</i>

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:35.720
I'm sorry, Akagi-kun, but it looks 
like this is the end for you.

00:14:36.050 --> 00:14:39.430
I can hear their voices...

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:43.730
The voices of the demons 
who rule Mahjong.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:48.740
The voices telling me to kill you.

00:14:57.020 --> 00:14:59.750
He's a... monster.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:03.440
Once Washizu's luck is set in motion,

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:05.250
it is beyond the understanding 
of ordinary minds.

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:08.810
Akagi's sense may be extraordinary,

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:12.260
but Washizu's luck goes 
to the utmost limit.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:16.570
<i>Anything can happen now.</i>

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:19.660
<i>It's godly.</i>

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:24.820
<i>Or perhaps the demons 
truly have possessed him.</i>

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:28.550
Shall we go on?

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:34.180
Before I draw my winning 
tile from the dead wall,

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:36.950
let's see the new dora indicator.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:42.970
<i>Now, take me higher.</i>

00:15:42.970 --> 00:15:45.520
<i>To an inconceivably high place.</i>

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:54.700
<i>Take me higher... higher and higher!</i>

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:14.690
Look at this, Akagi-kun.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:21.160
This is what the will of the demons 
who rule Mahjong looks like.

00:16:22.390 --> 00:16:24.160
What?

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.680
Another 1 of bamboo?!

00:16:26.680 --> 00:16:30.200
Wh-Which means... 12 dora?!

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:33.800
This is impossible!

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:36.990
How can this happen?!

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:43.010
They're pushing down on me 
with an unbelievable force.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:47.150
They're pushing down on my back.

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:50.260
They're here.

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:55.070
Something beyond description 
is on my back right now.

00:16:56.350 --> 00:17:00.080
Something demonic 
from the netherworld.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:08.730
They're gathered in great numbers 
and swarming around my back.

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:18.510
This old body can't 
hold itself up anymore.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:22.330
They're heavy... so heavy!

00:17:23.580 --> 00:17:27.360
It hurts... it hurts!

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:29.750
Ah, it hurts!

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:29.760
Washizu-sama!

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:41.240
Evil spirits...

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:53.230
Look, Akagi...

00:17:53.230 --> 00:17:57.490
I am truly possessed by demons now.

00:17:57.980 --> 00:18:02.490
Anything is possible for me now.

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:04.880
Now it is inevitable.

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:08.500
It is inevitable that I 
draw the winning tile.

00:18:08.830 --> 00:18:11.930
Which means you will die,

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:14.500
Akagi Shigeru.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:19.740
I'm not talking big here.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.810
I'm certain you know.

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.750
You can feel it.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.040
If anyone can understand it, it's you.

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:36.760
With a dealer baiman, you'll have 
lost a total of 1,900 CCs of blood.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:41.760
You would have a tiny 
chance of survival.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:45.550
But I have 14 han in my hand right now.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:51.230
And with a dealer yakuman, 
you really don't stand a chance.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:56.780
Altogether, you would 
lose 2,700 CCs of blood.

00:18:56.780 --> 00:18:58.510
You'll die!

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:03.520
You have no choice but to die.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.520
Now Washizu reaches for 
the dead wall draw.

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:16.260
<i>I'll draw it and kill him.</i>

00:19:17.310 --> 00:19:19.080
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:23.380
<i>1 of circles, where are you, 1 of circles?</i>

00:19:23.380 --> 00:19:25.000
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:29.230
<i>Kill, kill.</i>

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:35.750
<i>I'll... kill... him.</i>

00:19:38.450 --> 00:19:40.900
<i>I'll kill him.</i>

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:43.490
<i>Where are you, 1 of circles?</i>

00:19:43.810 --> 00:19:49.650
<i>Come on out, my precious 1 of circles.</i>

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.520
<i>Where are you?</i>

00:19:52.520 --> 00:19:54.730
<i>Where?</i>

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:56.290
<i>Is this it?</i>

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:58.240
<i>The 1 of circles?</i>

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:02.470
<i>So where is the 1 of circles?</i>

00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:11.230
<i>Is this the one?</i>

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.490
This one?

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:20.490
What... is this chill I'm feeling?

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.490
Is this chill...

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:33.460
Was it summoned by the madness 
of this man possessed by evil?

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.760
At that moment, it was 
as if they could all see

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:42.010
the demons erupting from 
this old man's back.

00:20:42.940 --> 00:20:46.000
Everyone in the room could feel it.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:52.760
